{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima","id":1337924,"title":"Obscuring The Anima","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-25T21:05:23-07:00","id":1337924,"title":"Obscuring The Anima","content":"Is there any published item or charm, any edition, which allows a character to make their anima appear to be an anima of a different exalt type? Specifically to allow an exalt to masquerade as another type of exalt? Closest thing I have found is the Nishkriya Mask, but that just adds an anima banner to someone who didn't have one to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T21:17:07-07:00","id":1337925,"title":"","content":"I think there was an artifact in 2nd that allowed an exalt to gain access to the Night's ability to not have their motes spent count as periphreal for however long that ability lasted, but that's all I can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T21:33:15-07:00","id":1337927,"title":"","content":"Perfect mirror lets you display whatever essence manifestation you want, including animas. You can't replicate the effects though, the the appearance. Fire won't burn, a dusk anima won't rot anything...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T21:43:01-07:00","id":1337928,"title":"","content":"I thought there was a sidereal or sidereal martial arts charm that did something like that, but I don't have my books at hand to check right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12111-the_larz","name":"the_larz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T22:05:01-07:00","id":1337930,"title":"","content":"3E Lunars Manuscript preview has the Appearance Charm Essential Mirror Nature, which does exactly what you describe. As a bonus, they also get a Charm to put their own anima on someone else, so using both Charms together you can make anyone appear as any Exalt type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T00:48:07-07:00","id":1337941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337930#post1337930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3E Lunars Manuscript preview has the Appearance Charm Essential Mirror Nature, which does exactly what you describe. As a bonus, they also get a Charm to put their own anima on someone else, so using both Charms together you can make anyone appear as any Exalt type.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh, what is the second charm? I don\u00b4t remember it, although I haven\u00b4t read Lunars since March! That sounds awesome!<br /> <br /> And the cool thing about Essential Mirror Nature is that if you are in the form of any other Exalt, you can adopt her exact same anima banner. So, in the form of Ledaal Isena, you would display her exact same anima banner. That\u00b4s incredibly cool and useful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T01:28:05-07:00","id":1337944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337941#post1337941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, what is the second charm? I don\u00b4t remember it, although I haven\u00b4t read Lunars since March! That sounds awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div><b>False Moonrise Phantasm</b>. The Lunar may displace anima levels to a character marked with Devil's Eye Brand. Unexalted victims display the Lunar's banner, but exalts will flare <i>their </i>own banner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337941#post1337941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the cool thing about Essential Mirror Nature is that if you are in the form of any other Exalt, you can adopt her exact same anima banner. So, in the form of Ledaal Isena, you would display her exact same anima banner. That\u00b4s incredibly cool and useful</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also waive the cost, and the maintain the charm indefinitely while in the stolen shape. A definite must for long term infiltration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-26-2019, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T01:47:54-07:00","id":1337947,"title":"","content":"The sidereal martial art Prismatic Order of Creation has a charm called [Type] Exalt Ways, which allowed the user to mimic another exalt type's anima. I think I allowed you to copy mechanical effects too (Probably not the eclipse charm learning).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24967-general-trivia-kit","name":"General Trivia Kit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T03:09:36-07:00","id":1337948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Trivia Kit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337947#post1337947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidereal martial art Prismatic Order of Creation has a charm called [Type] Exalt Ways, which allowed the user to mimic another exalt type's anima. I think I allowed you to copy mechanical effects too (Probably not the eclipse charm learning).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah... Prismatic <i>Arrangement</i> of Creation in Scroll of the Monk (2.5ed). Yes; <i>each</i> purchase of the charm allowed mimicry of the anima banner and <i>its effects</i> (and some other benefits) for <i>one</i> type and caste (or aspect) of exalted for <i>five actions</i>. Not <i>ideal</i> for impersonations, but useful.<br /> <br /> It does explicitly state that knowing the charm does not allow learning otherwise forbidden charms.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> But, if we're using 2ed resources, well, <b>Disguise of the New Face</b> is a Terrestrial Circle spell in Book of Sorcery II (White Treatise) that transforms the target's appearance, voice, mannerisms, and anima to imitate somebody until the imposture is revealed, removed by the subject, or dispelled by the caster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-26-2019, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T06:05:52-07:00","id":1337965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337927#post1337927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect mirror lets you display whatever essence manifestation you want, including animas. You can't replicate the effects though, the the appearance. Fire won't burn, a dusk anima won't rot anything...</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's that from?<br /> <br /> <b>Disguise of the New Face </b>doesn't say anything about the anima.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T06:57:16-07:00","id":1337970,"title":"","content":"Core solar Larceny charm, upgrade to Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T07:02:59-07:00","id":1337972,"title":"","content":"I think in 2E Fiend Caste Infernals (called Penumbra Caste in 3E) can learn this Charm :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>ELDRITCH SECRETS MASTERY</b><br /> <br /> Cost: \u2014<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Illusion<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Loom-Snarling Deception<br /> The lies of the Ebon Dragon may fool even magical senses. This Charm is a permanent upgrade to its prerequisite. <b>Whenever it is active, this Charm ensures that the Infernal\u2019s magical traits appear to be whatever he wants them to be</b>. If he wishes to appear Essence 1, Essence sight sees him so. If he chooses to conceal that he is a creature of darkness, he can fool the celestial lions guarding the gates of Yu-Shan. <b>If he wishes to seem as though his motes have a Solar aspect, others know this to be so</b>. Overcoming this upgraded Illusion requires the usual means. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T07:09:49-07:00","id":1337973,"title":"","content":"We've also been told that the Infernals in 3e would no longer learn the Charms of the Yozis themselves - parts of their Charmset would take inspiration from the Yozis, in the same way that Abyssal Charms can go off in a Deathlord-y direction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T07:28:25-07:00","id":1337980,"title":"","content":"Charms are also generally weaker, and that is a very powerful charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T08:15:23-07:00","id":1337985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337925#post1337925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there was an artifact in 2nd that allowed an exalt to gain access to the Night's ability to not have their motes spent count as periphreal for however long that ability lasted, but that's all I can think of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you... read the question at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T08:36:38-07:00","id":1337987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337973#post1337973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've also been told that the Infernals in 3e would no longer learn the Charms of the Yozis themselves - parts of their Charmset would take inspiration from the Yozis, in the same way that Abyssal Charms can go off in a Deathlord-y direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've previously asked Vance about that Charm specifically and he said Fiends' ability to disguise their Anima is very likely to come back (the 3rd question in this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1309258#post1309258\">post</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-26-2019, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T15:48:46-07:00","id":1338055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337985#post1337985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you... read the question at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's the closest I could come up with sparky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T16:09:47-07:00","id":1338059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BunniRabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1337965#post1337965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's that from?<br /> <br /> <b>Disguise of the New Face </b>doesn't say anything about the anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in the very first paragraph of the spell.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Books of Sorcery II</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> DISGUISE OF THE NEW FACE<br /> Cost: 15m<br /> Target: Creature<br /> This spell weaves an illusion that makes the target look like someone else. It transforms not just the person\u2019s appearance, but her voice, mannerisms and even anima.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T17:22:44-07:00","id":1338076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337924-obscuring-the-anima?p=1338055#post1338055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that's the closest I could come up with sparky.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201dSparky?\u201d <span style=\"color:white\">[/10char]</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T20:55:23-07:00","id":1338099,"title":"","content":"Oadenol's Codex from 2E had a 3 dot hearthstone, the Gem of White Heat, that could be used to produce an imitation Fire Aspect anima. Presumably a similar hearthstone could have been made to imitate other terrestrial animas.<br /> <br /> That said, it doesn't suppress your own anima, just allows you to produce the Fire one by feeding motes directly into it, so you'd need to be careful of your own anima if you have one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[]